 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\n# diff() function breaks when using pre-matchings parameter\n\n#### MCVE Code Sample\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one, exp\nfrom sqlglot.diff import diff\n\n# Create two SQL expressions\nexpr_src = parse_one('SELECT 1')\nexpr_tgt = parse_one('SELECT 1, 2, 3, 4')\n\n# Try to diff with pre-matchings\nresult = diff(expr_src, expr_tgt, matchings=[(expr_src, expr_tgt)])\n\n# This fails with an error\n```\n\nWhen trying to use the `matchings` parameter in the `diff()` function, it fails to properly handle the pre-matched nodes. The function doesn't correctly process the matchings when comparing source and target expressions.\n\n#### Expected Output\nThe function should correctly use the pre-matchings to identify that the source and target expressions are already matched at certain points, resulting in a smaller set of differences.\n\n#### Reproduction Steps\n1. Create two SQL expressions with some similarities\n2. Try to use the `diff()` function with the `matchings` parameter\n3. The function fails to properly handle the pre-matchings\n\n#### Environment Info\n- sqlglot version: latest\n- Python version: 3.10\n\nThis issue affects any code that relies on the pre-matching functionality of the diff algorithm, which is important for more complex SQL transformations where you want to guide the diff process.\n</issue>\n",
